semantic_query_expansion.prompt_text:
Return JSON matching the supplied response schema. The queries object has one registered lane as each key and its concrete catalogue search query as the value. Generate a real query for every lane. Never return field descriptions or placeholder text. Queries are retrieval hypotheses, never historical facts or results. For a personal name or place, exact searches of supplied name variants are useful. For a thematic question use short native-language subject and geographic terms plus travel-book/catalogue vocabulary. Do not invent identities or undocumented archive records. Keep each query under 100 characters. QUESTION_JSON: {"target": "Kimolos", "purpose": "What do contemporary travellers and archival sources state about merchant anchorage and drinking-water supply on Kimolos (Argentiera)? Keep publication dates separate from event dates. Do not infer piracy from the presence of ships. Cite actual newly acquired passages and report unread sources, inaccessible repositories and historical-verification gaps.", "date_range": "1700-1801"}
SUPPLIED_NAME_OR_PLACE_VARIANTS_NOT_IDENTITY_PROOF: ["Argentiera", "Κίμωλος"]
Use the catalogue language of each lane: greek=Greek; travellers/british=English; venetian/italian_states=Italian; french/north_african=French; spanish_simancas=Spanish; ottoman=Turkish; dutch=Dutch; german=German. Do not merely copy Greek prose into foreign-language lanes. Preserve genuine supplied personal names as retrieval variants, without asserting identity.
